Inspect Nushell plumbing modules.

Usage:
  strap nu modules
  strap nu lib-dir
  strap nu env-line
  strap nu use-line strap
  strap nu path plumbing
  strap nu use-line plumbing
  strap nu source-line plumbing

The `strap` module re-exports grouped commands such as `strap state init`, `strap session new`, `strap agents list`, and `strap skills list`. The `plumbing` module contains Nu-first immutable state and context commands, including closure-based combinators such as `with-events`, `map-events`, `where-events`, and `with-extract`.

Example:
  use '/path/to/strap/nu/strap'
  strap state init | strap agents apply chat-concise

After adding `strap nu lib-dir` to `NU_LIB_DIRS`, this also works:
  use strap
  strap state init

Plumbing-only example:
  use '/path/to/strap/nu/plumbing.nu' *
  open state.json | with-events {|events| $events | where from == user }

Prefer `use-line`; `source-line` is retained for quick interactive experiments and compatibility.
